  "body": "### What is the expected enhancement?\n\nSince #893, the `FermionicOp.simplify` method preserves the order of terms within a label.\r\nWhile this allows it to commute with the `normal_ordered()` method, it means that the following case cannot be simplified:\r\n```python\r\n>>> from qiskit_nature.second_q.operators import FermionicOp\r\n>>> FermionicOp({\"+_1 -_0\": 1, \"-_0 +_1\": 1}).simplify()\r\nFermionicOp({'+_1 -_0': (1+0j), '-_0 +_1': (1+0j)}, num_spin_orbitals=2, )\r\n```\r\nIt would be nice to at a keyword argument to simplify which is more aggressive (i.e. allows reordering the terms; off by default) to enable full simplifications.",
